{title: Go, Tell It on the Mountain}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}

{label: Chorus}
[G]Go, [C]tell it on the [G]mountain,
[D7]Over the hills and [G]everywhere;
Go, [C]tell it on the [G]moun[Em]tain
That [C]Jesus [D7]Christ is [G]born.

While shepherds kept their watch[Em]ing
O'er [D7]silent flocks by [G]night,
Behold throughout the heav[Em]ens
There [A7]shone a holy [D7]light.

{label: Chorus}

The shepherds feared and trembled
When lo! above the earth
Rang out the angel chorus
That hailed our Savior's birth.

{label: Chorus}

Down in a lowly manger
The humble Christ was born,
And God sent us salvation
That blessed Christmas morn.

{label: Chorus}
